From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeremy Melanson <1080872+zish@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:58:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: let a GeckoView embedder keep the profile's keys under
 its secret

encriox's spike keeps Lockstore's keys under a key from its vault, in
place of a primary password (encri-firefox, stage 2's second round).
GeckoRuntimeSettings takes a ProfileSecretDelegate, which Gecko asks at
startup, ahead of profile-do-change, on its own thread: a JNI call from
SyncProfileKekAtStartup, so the app's main thread is never held. The
secret unlocks the profile's password KEK, or makes it the first time,
and every DEK still under a LocalKey is moved under it and the LocalKey
dropped. Without a secret, a KEK that exists stays locked and startup
carries on, so that what each store then does can be measured. Nothing
here refuses startup or deletes a key.

The secret does not go through the environment or the extras, which
GeckoView copies into every child process, and Gecko wipes the Java
copy once it has its own. GeckoRuntime.lockProfile and unlockProfile
lock and unlock the KEK mid-session, through privileged JS.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
